  "abstract_summary": "Personalized language agents choose both what to remember about a person and how to use that memory. We separate these choices when predicting unseen answers to known interview questions. On 1,768 tasks from 188 people, a concrete memory built from a verified interview prefix outscores a trait description by 0.0158...",
